      "id": "attribution",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original independent-transform benchmark",
      "description": "Original MIT scenes, projects and matrices by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors. No customer/third-party images. build_example.py renders the known image transform independently of feature extraction/matching. Evaluator never fits a homography. Center reprojection within three target pixels defines eligible geometric edges; maximum one-to-one cardinality defines repeatability and recall denominator. Ranked candidate duplicates consume precision but cannot add true positives. Legacy native ellipse-overlap evaluation is a separate metric; its functions are not Python-bound here. Wrong transform and empty features deliberately fail; pair budget deliberately errors. Native feature counts can vary with build/settings.",
